Bicycle helmets fall under heading 6506, which covers other headgear. Subheading 6506.10 covers safety headgear. Within it, 6506.10.30 covers safety headgear of plastics and 6506.10.60 covers other safety headgear, so the plastic-shell helmets go in 6506.10.30. The statistical suffixes under 6506.10.30 are 6506.10.3000 for the "Of plastics" line, and I believe the general category is 6506.10.30.00.

Some CBP rulings on bicycle helmets classify them in 6506.10.6030, which is "Other: Other" under safety headgear. Rulings on bicycle helmets with a plastic shell and EPS liner usually use 6506.10.60.30. So I am not certain between the two. The 6506.10.30 line is "Of rubber or plastics" and includes the statistical suffix 6506.10.3000, while 6506.10.60 is "Other" with 6506.10.6030 (Bicycle helmets) and 6506.10.6045 (Other). Since I recall that statistical suffix, I go with 6506.10.6030.

{"hts_code": "6506.10.6030", "reason": "Bicycle helmets with molded shells and EPS impact liners are safety headgear of heading 6506, classified in the subheading for bicycle helmets."}
